      "sequence_position": 18,
      "problem": "Let the function $f(x,y)$ be defined as\n\n$$\nf(x,y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+y},\\, & \\text{if}\\,-1<x<1,\\,0<y<1, \\\\ x\\operatorname{ln}⁡y,\\, & \\text{if}\\,-1<x<1,\\,1<y<2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen,\n\n$$\n{∬}_{(-1,1)\\times (0,2)}f(x,y)\\text{ }\\text{d}A=\n$$",
      "worked_solution": "First, notice that the rectangle $R$ can be represented as a union of two smaller rectangles, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}R & =(-1,1)\\times ((0,1)\\cup (1,2)) \\\\  & =((-1,1)\\times (0,1))\\cup ((-1,1)\\times (1,2)).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we can write\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{R}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A & ={∬}_{(-1,1)\\times (0,1)}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A+{∬}_{(-1,1)\\times (1,2)}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{(-1,1)\\times (0,1)}\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+y}\\text{ }\\text{d}A+{∬}_{(-1,1)\\times (1,2)}x\\operatorname{ln}⁡y\\,\\text{d}A.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
